From: Georg Richter <georg@mariadb.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:34:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Branch 3.4 after 3.4.11: Merge branch '3.4-tls' into 3.4
 (CONC-865)

The change that merge commit f583dfe4d2dd3eeceb889049fb0ce549cb4f5c05 of the 3.4 branch of
https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-c brought,
taken as it landed on that branch (the diff against its first parent).
The commits it merges, with their own messages:

----- b1895c06e0e682edec20b0e54ba94142a8bed899
Author: Georg Richter <georg@mariadb.com>
Date:   Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:26:23 +0100

CONC-865: Treat a server certificate without CA as MARIADB_TLS_VERIFY_TRUST

A server may legitimately send only its leaf certificate (RFC 8446,
4.4.2 allows omitting the trust anchor). MariaDB servers built with
wolfSSL do this, while OpenSSL-based servers append the CA from ssl_ca.
A client without that CA reported the chain differently per backend:
OpenSSL failed with MARIADB_TLS_VERIFY_UNKNOWN, GnuTLS accepted it only
if the leaf itself was self-signed.

Both backends now report a chain that cannot be anchored in the
client's trust store as MARIADB_TLS_VERIFY_TRUST, i.e. the same way as a
self-signed certificate:

- OpenSSL: X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_GET_ISSUER_CERT (2),
  X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_GET_ISSUER_CERT_LOCALLY (20) and
  X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE (21) are mapped to TRUST,
  in addition to the self-signed errors (18, 19).
- GnuTLS: GNUTLS_CERT_SIGNER_NOT_FOUND is reported as TRUST. The
  ma_gnutls_is_self_signed() check on the leaf is removed, since
  GnuTLS uses this flag for several different situations.

A leaf without CA therefore no longer produces a verification error.
Whether the connection is accepted is decided as before:
 - if ssl_ca/ssl_capath is set, my_auth.c aborts the connection;
 - on local connections TRUST is not requested, so nothing is checked;
 - otherwise verification is deferred to the password based proof.
Unmapped errors (e.g. unknown critical extensions) still give
MARIADB_TLS_VERIFY_UNKNOWN.

Related fixes:
- ma_pvio_tls_verify_server_cert(): the status was masked with the
  requested flags, which dropped PERIOD, REVOKED and UNKNOWN. Only
  soft findings (TRUST, HOST, FINGERPRINT) that were not requested are
  dropped now. The unmasked result stays in extension->tls_validation.
- my_auth.c: clear the verification error once verification passed or
  was deferred, so a stale CR_SSL_CONNECTION_ERROR is not reported.
- ma_get_cert() (GnuTLS): fix certificate leak on import failure.

Tests: add leaf-without-CA and OpenSSL error 2 tests, and an
"intermediate" mode in the dummy TLS server. Results no longer depend
on whether the dummy server host is considered local.
